/-! # A flat Noetherian model retaining a polynomial presentation

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 02JO (3), with finite relation-coefficient descent,
and Tag 00FN (blueprint: lem-sfb-flat-fp-presentation-noetherian-model).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

open scoped TensorProduct

universe u v

namespace Algebra

/-- A prescribed polynomial surjection onto a flat finitely presented algebra descends
with the algebra to a finite type integer subring, with all three model rings Noetherian.

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 02JO (3), lemma-flat-finite-presentation-limit-flat,
and Tag 00FN, lemma-Noetherian-permanence; retaining the surjection is the finite
relation-coefficient refinement (blueprint: lem-sfb-flat-fp-presentation-noetherian-model).

Proof:
1. By lem-weil-pbc-finite-presentation-surjection-kernel-fg, choose finitely many
   generators of the kernel of the given surjection. The quotient by them is A.
2. Let C be the integer subalgebra generated by their coefficients. The finite type
   integer subalgebras containing C form a nonempty directed system with colimit R,
   using lemma-nagata-ring-finite-type-subalgebras and its cofinal subsystem.
3. At T use the polynomial quotient B_T by the same relations. It is finitely
   presented, and its transition maps are base changes by
   lem-weil-pbc-polynomial-scalar-extension and
   lem-weil-pbc-tensor-quotient-base-change. The comparison to A sends r tensor [p]
   to r times pi(p), using def-weil-pbc-algebra-hom-quotient.
4. Apply lem-weil-pbc-colimit-flat-ring-map to C -> B_C over this directed system.
   The limit is R -> A and is flat by hypothesis, so a stage T_0 -> B_T_0 is flat.
   The transition inclusions themselves need not be flat.
5. Take R_0 = T_0, A_0 = B_T_0 and pi_0 the quotient surjection. Exchange tensor
   factors to obtain alpha. On pure tensors its compatibility is the displayed
   formula, hence it is the prescribed polynomial map by tensor generation
   (def-weil-pbc-module-tensor-product).
6. The integers are Noetherian (their ideals are principal). Apply
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra-noetherian successively to R_0, its finite
   polynomial ring and its quotient A_0. Empty variable and relation lists and
   the zero rings are allowed throughout.
-/
theorem exists_flat_fp_presentation_noetherian_model
    {R : Type u} {A : Type v} [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]
    [Module.Flat R A] [Algebra.FinitePresentation R A]
    (n : ℕ) (π : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R →ₐ[R] A) (hπ : Function.Surjective π) :
    ∃ (R₀ : Subalgebra ℤ R) (A₀ : Type u) (_ : CommRing A₀) (_ : Algebra R₀ A₀),
      R₀.FG ∧ Module.Flat R₀ A₀ ∧ Algebra.FinitePresentation R₀ A₀ ∧
      IsNoetherianRing R₀ ∧ IsNoetherianRing (MvPolynomial (Fin n) R₀) ∧
      IsNoetherianRing A₀ ∧
      ∃ (π₀ : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R₀ →ₐ[R₀] A₀), Function.Surjective π₀ ∧
        ∃ (α : @AlgEquiv R (A₀ ⊗[R₀] R) A _ _ _
            Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra _),
          ∀ (p : MvPolynomial (Fin n) R₀) (r : R),
            α (π₀ p ⊗ₜ[R₀] r) = r • π (MvPolynomial.map R₀.val.toRingHom p) := by
  sorry

end Algebra
